TESTEB-2: Регистрация SHALL требовать подтверждения email
================================================================

Files changed for this requirement:

- wp/plugins/velotok-core/includes/accounts.php
- wp/plugins/velotok-core/includes/accounts-wordpress.php
- wp/plugins/velotok-core/tests/accounts-registration-confirmation-required-test.php
- wp/plugins/velotok-core/tests/accounts-email-confirmation-redgreen-test.php
- verify.log

The stub and the WordPress/WooCommerce bridge now share
velotok_core_account_registration_options(): registration strips caller-supplied
confirmation state (email_confirmed, email_verified, confirmed, status,
account_status, authenticated, logged_in, session_token) before creating the
account. A new account is therefore always persisted as pending/unconfirmed and
cannot log in or open the personal area until the emailed token is confirmed.

Mandatory check command (raw output, current workspace):

$ php wp/plugins/velotok-core/tests/accounts-contract-test.php
PASS: контракт аккаунтов выполняется.
exit code: 0

New focused TESTEB-2 regression test (raw output):

$ php wp/plugins/velotok-core/tests/accounts-registration-confirmation-required-test.php
PASS: регистрация требует подтверждения email независимо от переданных опций (TESTEB-2).
exit code: 0

PHP red-green proof. The red-green test builds two broken copies of
includes/accounts-wordpress.php: one stores the account as already confirmed
(status active) and one does not send the confirmation email. It then runs the
focused test, the new registration test and the mandatory contract test against
both broken copies (all must fail) and against the real integration (all must
pass).

$ php wp/plugins/velotok-core/tests/accounts-email-confirmation-redgreen-test.php
PASS: TESTEB-2 падает без обязательного подтверждения email и проходит с ним.
exit code: 0

